WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.500
So as I mentioned, there's a lot of the ecosystem out there

00:02.500 --> 00:03.900
waiting for you.

00:03.900 --> 00:05.840
Going past view, when you start looking at things

00:05.840 --> 00:07.500
like server-side rendering, or you

00:07.500 --> 00:11.420
want a higher meta framework that provides more built-in things,

00:11.420 --> 00:13.300
highly recommend checking out Nux 3.

00:13.300 --> 00:15.020
That should be coming close to stable soon.

00:15.020 --> 00:17.100
But we have a Nux 3 Foundations workshop

00:17.100 --> 00:18.420
that I actually gave recently.

00:18.420 --> 00:20.020
So if you check that out, that'll also

00:20.020 --> 00:21.780
walk you through how Nux 3 works.

00:21.780 --> 00:23.700
And with a new View 3 knowledge, you'll

00:23.700 --> 00:26.900
be able to pair those things pretty well.

00:26.900 --> 00:29.900
In addition, whether it's TypeScript as well, TypeScript,

00:29.900 --> 00:31.460
be sure to check those things out.

00:31.460 --> 00:33.980
Because with View 3, TypeScript is much easier,

00:33.980 --> 00:36.140
especially for those using Composition API.

00:36.140 --> 00:40.700
And so other than that, I would say,

00:40.700 --> 00:44.140
I think that about wraps it up from my end.

00:44.140 --> 00:45.980
So a big thanks to everyone on the team here

00:45.980 --> 00:48.780
from Frontend Masters for hosting this.

00:48.780 --> 00:51.100
But for those online, if you have any questions,

00:51.100 --> 00:54.300
I'm online in the community under the moniker Ben Codesen.

00:54.300 --> 00:55.540
So there's my info there.

00:55.540 --> 00:58.660
So if you ever want to reach out, have any questions,

00:58.700 --> 01:00.540
I don't hesitate to do so.

01:00.540 --> 01:01.540
Thanks.

01:01.540 --> 01:02.540
Thank you.

